(NULL, '2000168', '168', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain: a clinical epidemiology analysis', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2024', 'Researchers evaluated a graded activity programme against standard care in 422 adults with chronic low back pain. The primary analysis indicated a modest improvement for pain-related function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The analysis was designed to reflect the decisions faced by clinicians in routine practice.', '2025-02-20 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0168', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000066', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000169', '169', 'Correction: A Graded Activity Programme and pain-related function in chronic low back pain: an assessment of variation in response', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2026', 'This notice corrects a nonclinical metadata error in an earlier report on a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain. The participant population, intervention, comparator, analyses, and clinical conclusions are unchanged. The corrected record clarifies the outcome definition and preserves the original study context for evidence review. A prespecified sensitivity analysis produced estimates in the same general direction.', '2025-01-21 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0169', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000066', 'Correction: A Graded Activity Programme and pain-related function in chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000170', '170', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a service-user experience report', 'Marta Kowalski//Jonas Berg//Lucia Ferraro', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2022', 'an outpatient research network tested structured medication review for adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Participants will be recruited at urban and regional clinical sites; the planned sample is 459 and symptom burden is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. The report distinguishes protocol-defined outcomes from exploratory measures collected during follow-up.', '2025-02-09 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0170', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000067', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000171', '171', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a longitudinal safety analysis', 'Marta Kowalski//Jonas Berg//Lucia Ferraro', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'The trial team compared structured medication review against standard care in 459 adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. The observed difference was clinically interpretable for symptom burden, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. Differences in adherence were more pronounced among participants recruited through community services.', '2025-01-10 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0171', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000067', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000172', '172', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for guided behavioural activation in major depressive disorder: a study of implementation fidelity', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2023', 'an outpatient research network tested guided behavioural activation for adults with major depressive disorder. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 496 and depressive symptom severity is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The investigators noted that the observed association should not be interpreted as proof of causation.', '2025-01-29 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0172', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000068', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for guided behavioural activation in major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000173', '173', 'A pragmatic evaluation of guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder: a comparison across recruitment settings', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'A multicentre investigation examined guided behavioural activation against standard care in 496 adults with major depressive disorder. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for depressive symptom severity, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The study team documented variation in delivery intensity across participating sites.', '2025-02-17 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0173', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000068', 'A pragmatic evaluation of guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000174', '174', 'Who benefits from guided behavioural activation? A subgroup analysis in major depressive disorder: an analysis of resource use', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'Trials', '2025', 'This analysis explored heterogeneity of response to guided behavioural activation in adults with major depressive disorder. Improvement in depressive symptom severity was observed across several prespecified strata, with the largest estimates among participants with greater baseline impairment. The findings are exploratory and require confirmation in independent cohorts. Results were broadly stable after adjustment for age, baseline severity, and prior treatment. The analysis separated scheduled contacts from unscheduled healthcare use.', '2025-01-17 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0174', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000068', 'Who benefits from guided behavioural activation? A subgroup analysis in major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000175', '175', 'Adverse events and treatment exposure during guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder: a report on treatment acceptability', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'Safety data from the evaluation of guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder were reviewed across 496 participants. Most events were mild or unrelated to treatment; serious events were uncommon and balanced between groups. Exposure, discontinuation, and protocol deviations are reported to support interpretation of the clinical outcome findings. The report discusses how missing observations may affect interpretation of the final estimates.', '2025-02-06 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0175', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000068', 'Adverse events and treatment exposure during guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000176', '176', 'Comparative effectiveness of home strength and balance exercise for postoperative joint replacement recovery: a pragmatic registry analysis', 'Amara Williams//Diego Alvarez//Ines Pereira', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'Researchers evaluated home strength and balance exercise against standard care in 113 adults with postoperative joint replacement recovery. Between-group estimates favoured the intervention for functional mobility, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The findings are intended to inform evidence synthesis rather than replace confirmatory trials.', '2025-01-06 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0176', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000069', 'Comparative effectiveness of home strength and balance exercise for postoperative joint replacement recovery', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000177', '177', 'Implementing personalised dietary counselling in routine care for hypertension: a study of care access and outcomes', 'Noor Rahman//Ethan Cole//Maya Singh', 'Trials', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of personalised dietary counselling for people with hypertension across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside systolic blood pressure. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The analysis also considered differences between hospital and community delivery settings. The report included a prespecified comparison of urban and regional recruitment settings.', '2025-01-25 09:00:00', '2026-07-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0177', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000070', 'Implementing personalised dietary counselling in routine care for hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000178', '178', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy: an analysis of longer-term use', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'This baseline report describes 187 adults enrolled to assess brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults. Participants were recruited at urban and regional clinical sites; baseline severity, medication use, functional status, and social factors were recorded before treatment allocation. The cohort was broadly representative of the intended clinical population, although referral patterns may affect external validity. Recruitment pathways and treatment fidelity were examined to support interpretation of the estimates.', '2025-02-14 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0178', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000179', '179', 'A pragmatic evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults: a report on clinical decision-making', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'An outpatient research network tested brief sleep restriction therapy against standard care in 187 adults with insomnia in older adults. The primary analysis indicated a modest improvement for sleep efficiency, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. The report includes a sensitivity analysis using an alternative definition of the primary outcome.', '2025-01-14 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0179', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'A pragmatic evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000180', '180', 'Patient-reported experience after brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults: a multisite patient follow-up', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'This report examined patient-reported experience and quality of life after brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults. Participants described changes in daily activity, confidence, symptom control, and care burden. Improvements in sleep efficiency were accompanied by variable satisfaction with access and treatment workload. Patient retention varied by site, with the largest losses occurring before the final assessment.', '2025-02-02 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0180', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'Patient-reported experience after brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000181', '181', 'Implementing brief sleep restriction therapy in routine care for insomnia in older adults: evidence from participating centres', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of brief sleep restriction therapy for people with insomnia in older adults across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside sleep efficiency. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Results were interpreted alongside baseline severity, treatment exposure, and concurrent care.', '2025-02-21 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0181', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'Implementing brief sleep restriction therapy in routine care for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000182', '182', 'Implementing brief sleep restriction therapy in routine care for insomnia in older adults: a pragmatic service evaluation', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'Trials', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of brief sleep restriction therapy for people with insomnia in older adults across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside sleep efficiency. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The investigators reported uncertainty intervals rather than relying on a single summary estimate.', '2025-01-22 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0182', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'Implementing brief sleep restriction therapy in routine care for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000183', '183', 'Adverse events and treatment exposure during brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults: findings from routine clinical practice', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'BMJ Open', '2026', 'Safety data from the evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults were reviewed across 187 participants. Most events were mild or unrelated to treatment; serious events were uncommon and balanced between groups. Exposure, discontinuation, and protocol deviations are reported to support interpretation of the clinical outcome findings. Service capacity and local referral practices influenced the observed pattern of care.', '2025-02-10 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0183', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000071', 'Adverse events and treatment exposure during brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000184', '184', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a longitudinal cohort analysis', 'Amina Okafor//Luis Martinez//Priya Nair', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of pacing and energy conservation coaching for people with post-viral fatigue syndrome across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside physical function. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The analysis was designed to reflect the decisions faced by clinicians in routine practice.', '2025-01-11 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0184', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000072', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000186', '186', 'Implementing home pulmonary rehabilitation in routine care for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: a community-based assessment', 'Mei Chen//Daniel Brooks//Fatima Haddad', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of home pulmonary rehabilitation for people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside exercise tolerance. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The report distinguishes protocol-defined outcomes from exploratory measures collected during follow-up.', '2025-02-18 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0186', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000074', 'Implementing home pulmonary rehabilitation in routine care for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000187', '187', 'Implementing a graded activity programme in routine care for chronic low back pain: a patient-centred outcomes report', 'Tunde Adeyemi//Elena Novak//Rafael Silva', 'Trials', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of a graded activity programme for people with chronic low back pain across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside pain-related function. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Differences in adherence were more pronounced among participants recruited through community services.', '2025-01-19 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0187', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000075', 'Implementing a graded activity programme in routine care for chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000188', '188', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: results from linked clinical records', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'BMJ Open', '2023', 'investigators explored structured medication review for adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 372 and symptom burden is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. The investigators noted that the observed association should not be interpreted as proof of causation.', '2025-02-07 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0188', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000076', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000189', '189', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a mixed-methods implementation report', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2024', 'This prospective study assessed structured medication review against standard care in 372 adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for symptom burden, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. The study team documented variation in delivery intensity across participating sites.', '2025-01-07 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0189', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000076', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000190', '190', 'Implementing structured medication review in routine care for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a multisite effectiveness study', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of structured medication review for people with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside symptom burden. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Results were broadly stable after adjustment for age, baseline severity, and prior treatment.', '2025-01-27 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0190', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000076', 'Implementing structured medication review in routine care for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000191', '191', 'Budget impact ofstructured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a prespecified analysis of outcomes', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'A within-trial economic evaluation estimated healthcare use and costs associated with structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Resource use, service contacts, medication changes, and quality-adjusted survival were compared with standard care. Results were sensitive to assumptions about intervention delivery and longer-term maintenance. Results depended most strongly on the assumed rate of continued service use after the study period.', '2025-02-15 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0191', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000076', 'Health-service costs associated with structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000192', '192', 'Secondary analysis of symptom burden after structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a health-system perspective', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'Trials', '2025', 'A prespecified secondary analysis examined variation in symptom burden after structured medication review among adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Effects were explored by baseline severity, age, adherence, and recruitment setting. The pattern was directionally consistent with the primary analysis, but subgroup estimates were imprecise. The findings are intended to inform evidence synthesis rather than replace confirmatory trials.', '2025-01-15 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0192', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000076', 'Secondary analysis of symptom burden after structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000193', '193', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for guided behavioural activation in major depressive disorder: a follow-up analysis of care pathways', 'Nadia Hassan//Samuel Reed//Chloe Dubois', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2024', 'this prospective study assessed guided behavioural activation for adults with major depressive disorder. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 409 and depressive symptom severity is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. The analysis also considered differences between hospital and community delivery settings.', '2025-02-04 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0193', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000077', 'Protocol And Statistical Analysis Plan for guided behavioural activation in major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000194', '194', 'Clinical outcomes after guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder: an outpatient outcomes study', 'Nadia Hassan//Samuel Reed//Chloe Dubois', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'This prospective study assessed guided behavioural activation against standard care in 409 adults with major depressive disorder. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for depressive symptom severity, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. Recruitment pathways and treatment fidelity were examined to support interpretation of the estimates.', '2025-02-23 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0194', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000077', 'Clinical outcomes after guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000195', '195', 'Clinical outcomes after guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder: a real-world assessment of delivery', 'Nadia Hassan//Samuel Reed//Chloe Dubois', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'Investigators explored guided behavioural activation against standard care in 409 adults with major depressive disorder. The observed difference was clinically interpretable for depressive symptom severity, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The report includes a sensitivity analysis using an alternative definition of the primary outcome.', '2025-01-23 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0195', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000077', 'Clinical outcomes after guided behavioural activation for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
