(NULL, '2000202', '202', 'Comparative effectiveness of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension: a study of implementation fidelity', 'Marta Kowalski//Jonas Berg//Lucia Ferraro', 'Trials', '2025', 'The trial team compared personalised dietary counselling against standard care in 483 adults with hypertension. Between-group estimates favoured the intervention for systolic blood pressure, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. The report distinguishes protocol-defined outcomes from exploratory measures collected during follow-up.', '2025-01-09 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0202', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000079', 'Comparative effectiveness of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000203', '203', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy: a comparison across recruitment settings', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'Trials', '2025', 'This baseline report describes 100 adults enrolled to assess brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults. Participants were recruited across community services and outpatient practices; baseline severity, medication use, functional status, and social factors were recorded before treatment allocation. The cohort was broadly representative of the intended clinical population, although referral patterns may affect external validity. Differences in adherence were more pronounced among participants recruited through community services.', '2025-01-28 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0203', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000080', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000204', '204', 'A pragmatic evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults: an analysis of resource use', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'BMJ Open', '2024', 'Investigators explored brief sleep restriction therapy against standard care in 100 adults with insomnia in older adults. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for sleep efficiency, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The investigators noted that the observed association should not be interpreted as proof of causation.', '2025-02-16 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0204', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000080', 'A pragmatic evaluation of brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000205', '205', 'Correction: Brief Sleep Restriction Therapy and sleep efficiency in insomnia in older adults: a report on treatment acceptability', 'Zainab Bello//Thomas Wright//Yuki Tanaka', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2026', 'This notice corrects a nonclinical metadata error in an earlier report on brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults. The participant population, intervention, comparator, analyses, and clinical conclusions are unchanged. The corrected record clarifies the outcome definition and preserves the original study context for evidence review. The study team documented variation in delivery intensity across participating sites.', '2025-01-17 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0205', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000080', 'Correction: Brief Sleep Restriction Therapy and sleep efficiency in insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000206', '206', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a pragmatic registry analysis', 'Amara Williams//Diego Alvarez//Ines Pereira', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of pacing and energy conservation coaching for people with post-viral fatigue syndrome across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside physical function. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Results were broadly stable after adjustment for age, baseline severity, and prior treatment.', '2025-02-05 09:00:00', '2026-02-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0206', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000081', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000207', '207', 'Comparative effectiveness of home blood pressure monitoring for hypertension: a study of care access and outcomes', 'Noor Rahman//Ethan Cole//Maya Singh', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'This prospective study assessed home blood pressure monitoring against standard care in 174 adults with hypertension. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for glycaemic control, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. The report discusses how missing observations may affect interpretation of the final estimates.', '2025-02-24 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0207', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000082', 'Comparative effectiveness of home blood pressure monitoring for hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000208', '208', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for home pulmonary rehabilitation in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: an analysis of longer-term use', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2022', 'the trial team compared home pulmonary rehabilitation for adults with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Participants will be recruited using electronic records and clinician referral; the planned sample is 211 and exercise tolerance is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. The findings are intended to inform evidence synthesis rather than replace confirmatory trials.', '2025-01-24 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0208', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000083', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for home pulmonary rehabilitation in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000209', '209', 'A pragmatic evaluation of home pulmonary rehabilitation for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: a report on clinical decision-making', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'Researchers evaluated home pulmonary rehabilitation against standard care in 211 adults with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. The observed difference was clinically interpretable for exercise tolerance, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The analysis also considered differences between hospital and community delivery settings.', '2025-02-13 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0209', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000083', 'A pragmatic evaluation of home pulmonary rehabilitation for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000210', '210', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain: a multisite patient follow-up', 'Amina Okafor//Luis Martinez//Priya Nair', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'A multicentre investigation examined a graded activity programme against standard care in 248 adults with chronic low back pain. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for pain-related function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. Recruitment pathways and treatment fidelity were examined to support interpretation of the estimates.', '2025-01-13 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0210', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000084', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000211', '211', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: evidence from participating centres', 'Kwame Mensah//Sofia Rossi//Hannah Wilson', 'Trials', '2024', 'the trial team compared structured medication review for adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Participants will be recruited across community services and outpatient practices; the planned sample is 285 and symptom burden is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The report includes a sensitivity analysis using an alternative definition of the primary outcome.', '2025-02-01 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0211', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000085', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000212', '212', 'Implementing guided behavioural activation in routine care for major depressive disorder: a pragmatic service evaluation', 'Mei Chen//Daniel Brooks//Fatima Haddad', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of guided behavioural activation for people with major depressive disorder across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside depressive symptom severity. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Patient retention varied by site, with the largest losses occurring before the final assessment.', '2025-02-20 09:00:00', '2026-07-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0212', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000086', 'Implementing guided behavioural activation in routine care for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000213', '213', 'A pragmatic evaluation of home strength and balance exercise for postoperative joint replacement recovery: findings from routine clinical practice', 'Tunde Adeyemi//Elena Novak//Rafael Silva', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2024', 'A multicentre investigation examined home strength and balance exercise against standard care in 359 adults with postoperative joint replacement recovery. Between-group estimates favoured the intervention for functional mobility, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. Results were interpreted alongside baseline severity, treatment exposure, and concurrent care.', '2025-01-21 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0213', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000087', 'A pragmatic evaluation of home strength and balance exercise for postoperative joint replacement recovery', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000214', '214', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of personalised dietary counselling: a longitudinal cohort analysis', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2024', 'This baseline report describes 396 adults enrolled to assess personalised dietary counselling for hypertension. Participants were recruited across community services and outpatient practices; baseline severity, medication use, functional status, and social factors were recorded before treatment allocation. The cohort was broadly representative of the intended clinical population, although referral patterns may affect external validity. The investigators reported uncertainty intervals rather than relying on a single summary estimate.', '2025-02-09 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0214', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000088', 'Baseline characteristics of adults enrolled in an evaluation of personalised dietary counselling', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000215', '215', 'A pragmatic evaluation of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension: a participant-level secondary analysis', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'This prospective study assessed personalised dietary counselling against standard care in 396 adults with hypertension. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for systolic blood pressure, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. Service capacity and local referral practices influenced the observed pattern of care.', '2025-01-10 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0215', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000088', 'A pragmatic evaluation of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000216', '216', 'Prospective Study Protocol for brief sleep restriction therapy in insomnia in older adults: a community-based assessment', 'Nadia Hassan//Samuel Reed//Chloe Dubois', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'a multicentre investigation examined brief sleep restriction therapy for adults with insomnia in older adults. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 433 and sleep efficiency is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The analysis was designed to reflect the decisions faced by clinicians in routine practice.', '2025-01-29 09:00:00', '2026-02-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0216', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000089', 'Prospective Study Protocol for brief sleep restriction therapy in insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000217', '217', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for pacing and energy conservation coaching in post-viral fatigue syndrome: a patient-centred outcomes report', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Trials', '2025', 'an outpatient research network tested pacing and energy conservation coaching for adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. Participants will be recruited through primary-care and specialist clinics; the planned sample is 470 and physical function is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. A prespecified sensitivity analysis produced estimates in the same general direction.', '2025-02-17 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0217', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for pacing and energy conservation coaching in post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000218', '218', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: results from linked clinical records', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'BMJ Open', '2024', 'Investigators explored pacing and energy conservation coaching against standard care in 470 adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. The observed difference was clinically interpretable for physical function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The report distinguishes protocol-defined outcomes from exploratory measures collected during follow-up.', '2025-01-18 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0218', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000219', '219', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a mixed-methods implementation report', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of pacing and energy conservation coaching for people with post-viral fatigue syndrome across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside physical function. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Differences in adherence were more pronounced among participants recruited through community services.', '2025-02-06 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0219', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000220', '220', 'A pragmatic evaluation of pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a multisite effectiveness study', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2024', 'This prospective study assessed pacing and energy conservation coaching against standard care in 470 adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. The primary analysis indicated a modest improvement for physical function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The investigators noted that the observed association should not be interpreted as proof of causation.', '2025-01-06 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0220', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'A pragmatic evaluation of pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000221', '221', 'Patient-reported experience after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a prespecified analysis of outcomes', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'This report examined patient-reported experience and quality of life after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. Participants described changes in daily activity, confidence, symptom control, and care burden. Improvements in physical function were accompanied by variable satisfaction with access and treatment workload. The study team documented variation in delivery intensity across participating sites.', '2025-01-26 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0221', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Patient-reported experience after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000222', '222', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a health-system perspective', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Trials', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of pacing and energy conservation coaching for people with post-viral fatigue syndrome across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside physical function. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. Results were broadly stable after adjustment for age, baseline severity, and prior treatment. The investigators recorded how referral source influenced service use during follow-up.', '2025-02-14 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0222', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Implementing pacing and energy conservation coaching in routine care for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000223', '223', 'Budget impact ofpacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a follow-up analysis of care pathways', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'A within-trial economic evaluation estimated healthcare use and costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. Resource use, service contacts, medication changes, and quality-adjusted survival were compared with standard care. Results were sensitive to assumptions about intervention delivery and longer-term maintenance. Costs were separated into intervention delivery, primary care, hospital care, and medication use.', '2025-01-14 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0223', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Health-service costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000224', '224', 'Who benefits from pacing and energy conservation coaching? A subgroup analysis in post-viral fatigue syndrome: an outpatient outcomes study', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'This analysis explored heterogeneity of response to pacing and energy conservation coaching in adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. Improvement in physical function was observed across several prespecified strata, with the largest estimates among participants with greater baseline impairment. The findings are exploratory and require confirmation in independent cohorts. The findings are intended to inform evidence synthesis rather than replace confirmatory trials.', '2025-02-03 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0224', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Who benefits from pacing and energy conservation coaching? A subgroup analysis in post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000225', '225', 'Resource use and cost consequences ofpacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a real-world assessment of delivery', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'A within-trial economic evaluation estimated healthcare use and costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. Resource use, service contacts, medication changes, and quality-adjusted survival were compared with standard care. Results were sensitive to assumptions about intervention delivery and longer-term maintenance. Cost estimates were presented from the healthcare-system perspective and in sensitivity analyses from a wider societal perspective.', '2025-02-22 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0225', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Health-service costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000226', '226', 'Patient-reported experience after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: an analysis of treatment persistence', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'This report examined patient-reported experience and quality of life after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. Participants described changes in daily activity, confidence, symptom control, and care burden. Improvements in physical function were accompanied by variable satisfaction with access and treatment workload. Recruitment pathways and treatment fidelity were examined to support interpretation of the estimates. The authors described uncertainty around maintenance of the observed pattern beyond follow-up.', '2025-01-22 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0226', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Patient-reported experience after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000227', '227', 'A pragmatic evaluation of pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a report from regional services', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Trials', '2025', 'The trial team compared pacing and energy conservation coaching against standard care in 470 adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for physical function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. The report includes a sensitivity analysis using an alternative definition of the primary outcome.', '2025-02-10 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0227', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'A pragmatic evaluation of pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000228', '228', 'Cost-effectiveness ofpacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a clinical epidemiology analysis', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'A within-trial economic evaluation estimated healthcare use and costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. Resource use, service contacts, medication changes, and quality-adjusted survival were compared with standard care. Results were sensitive to assumptions about intervention delivery and longer-term maintenance. The analysis reported both observed trial costs and projected costs over a longer decision horizon.', '2025-01-11 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0228', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Health-service costs associated with pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000229', '229', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: an assessment of variation in response', 'Arjun Mehta//Grace Kim//Peter Osei', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2025', 'The trial team compared pacing and energy conservation coaching against standard care in 470 adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for physical function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. Results were interpreted alongside baseline severity, treatment exposure, and concurrent care.', '2025-01-30 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0229', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000090', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
