(NULL, '2000235', '235', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain: a report on treatment acceptability', 'Amara Williams//Diego Alvarez//Ines Pereira', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'This prospective study assessed a graded activity programme against standard care in 161 adults with chronic low back pain. Between-group estimates favoured the intervention for pain-related function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. Differences in adherence were more pronounced among participants recruited through community services.', '2025-02-15 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0235', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000093', 'Comparative effectiveness of a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000236', '236', 'Correction: A Graded Activity Programme and pain-related function in chronic low back pain: a pragmatic registry analysis', 'Amara Williams//Diego Alvarez//Ines Pereira', 'Trials', '2026', 'This notice corrects a nonclinical metadata error in an earlier report on a graded activity programme for chronic low back pain. The participant population, intervention, comparator, analyses, and clinical conclusions are unchanged. The corrected record clarifies the outcome definition and preserves the original study context for evidence review. The investigators noted that the observed association should not be interpreted as proof of causation.', '2025-01-16 09:00:00', '2026-06-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0236', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000093', 'Correction: A Graded Activity Programme and pain-related function in chronic low back pain', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000237', '237', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: a study of care access and outcomes', 'Noor Rahman//Ethan Cole//Maya Singh', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2025', 'the trial team compared structured medication review for adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 198 and symptom burden is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. The study team documented variation in delivery intensity across participating sites.', '2025-02-04 09:00:00', '2026-07-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0237', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000094', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for structured medication review in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000238', '238', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: an analysis of longer-term use', 'Noor Rahman//Ethan Cole//Maya Singh', 'Trials', '2024', 'An outpatient research network tested structured medication review against standard care in 198 adults with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for symptom burden, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. Results were broadly stable after adjustment for age, baseline severity, and prior treatment.', '2025-02-23 09:00:00', '2026-07-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0238', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000094', 'Comparative effectiveness of structured medication review for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000239', '239', 'Implementing guided behavioural activation in routine care for major depressive disorder: a report on clinical decision-making', 'Aisha Grant//Victor Petrov//Clara Martin', 'Trials', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of guided behavioural activation for people with major depressive disorder across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside depressive symptom severity. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The report discusses how missing observations may affect interpretation of the final estimates.', '2025-01-23 09:00:00', '2026-08-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0239', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000095', 'Implementing guided behavioural activation in routine care for major depressive disorder', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000240', '240', 'Implementing home strength and balance exercise in routine care for postoperative joint replacement recovery: a multisite patient follow-up', 'Amina Okafor//Luis Martinez//Priya Nair', 'BMJ Open', '2025', 'This implementation report describes delivery of home strength and balance exercise for people with postoperative joint replacement recovery across routine services. Staff training, referral pathways, fidelity, reach, and participant engagement were monitored alongside functional mobility. Adoption was feasible, although local staffing and infrastructure shaped delivery. The findings are intended to inform evidence synthesis rather than replace confirmatory trials. The investigators noted that the findings are most applicable to services with similar staffing.', '2025-02-12 09:00:00', '2026-01-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0240', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000096', 'Implementing home strength and balance exercise in routine care for postoperative joint replacement recovery', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000241', '241', 'Comparative effectiveness of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension: evidence from participating centres', 'Kwame Mensah//Sofia Rossi//Hannah Wilson', 'Journal of Clinical Epidemiology', '2024', 'Researchers evaluated personalised dietary counselling against standard care in 309 adults with hypertension. Results were consistent with the prespecified hypothesis for systolic blood pressure, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. The analysis also considered differences between hospital and community delivery settings.', '2025-01-12 09:00:00', '2026-02-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0241', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000097', 'Comparative effectiveness of personalised dietary counselling for hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000242', '242', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for brief sleep restriction therapy in insomnia in older adults: a pragmatic service evaluation', 'Mei Chen//Daniel Brooks//Fatima Haddad', 'The Lancet Regional Health', '2025', 'a multicentre investigation examined brief sleep restriction therapy for adults with insomnia in older adults. Participants will be recruited through primary-care and specialist clinics; the planned sample is 346 and sleep efficiency is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. Recruitment pathways and treatment fidelity were examined to support interpretation of the estimates.', '2025-01-31 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Open-label pilot study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0242', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000098', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for brief sleep restriction therapy in insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000243', '243', 'Clinical outcomes after brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults: findings from routine clinical practice', 'Mei Chen//Daniel Brooks//Fatima Haddad', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2024', 'Researchers evaluated brief sleep restriction therapy against standard care in 346 adults with insomnia in older adults. The primary analysis indicated a modest improvement for sleep efficiency, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Interpretation is limited by attrition and the pragmatic delivery setting. The report includes a sensitivity analysis using an alternative definition of the primary outcome.', '2025-02-19 09:00:00', '2026-03-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0243', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000098', 'Clinical outcomes after brief sleep restriction therapy for insomnia in older adults', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000244', '244', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for pacing and energy conservation coaching in post-viral fatigue syndrome: a longitudinal cohort analysis', 'Tunde Adeyemi//Elena Novak//Rafael Silva', 'BMC Health Services Research', '2022', 'investigators explored pacing and energy conservation coaching for adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. Participants will be recruited using electronic records and clinician referral; the planned sample is 383 and physical function is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. Patient retention varied by site, with the largest losses occurring before the final assessment.', '2025-01-20 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Parallel-group randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0244', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000099', 'Registered Protocol For The Planned Evaluation for pacing and energy conservation coaching in post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000245', '245', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome: a participant-level secondary analysis', 'Tunde Adeyemi//Elena Novak//Rafael Silva', 'Trials', '2025', 'The trial team compared pacing and energy conservation coaching against standard care in 383 adults with post-viral fatigue syndrome. The observed difference was clinically interpretable for physical function, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. The findings should be considered alongside short follow-up and incomplete adherence data. Results were interpreted alongside baseline severity, treatment exposure, and concurrent care.', '2025-02-08 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '2', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0245', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000099', 'Clinical outcomes after pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000246', '246', 'Correction: Pacing And Energy Conservation Coaching and physical function in post-viral fatigue syndrome: a community-based assessment', 'Tunde Adeyemi//Elena Novak//Rafael Silva', 'BMJ Open', '2026', 'This notice corrects a nonclinical metadata error in an earlier report on pacing and energy conservation coaching for post-viral fatigue syndrome. The participant population, intervention, comparator, analyses, and clinical conclusions are unchanged. The corrected record clarifies the outcome definition and preserves the original study context for evidence review. The investigators reported uncertainty intervals rather than relying on a single summary estimate. The authors described uncertainty around maintenance of the observed pattern beyond follow-up.', '2025-01-09 09:00:00', '2026-04-15 00:00:00', '4', '1', 'Prospective cohort study', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0246', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000099', 'Correction: Pacing And Energy Conservation Coaching and physical function in post-viral fatigue syndrome', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press'),
(NULL, '2000247', '247', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for home blood pressure monitoring in hypertension: a patient-centred outcomes report, report 247', 'Leila Ibrahim//Marcus Thompson//Keiko Yamamoto', 'Trials', '2023', 'investigators explored home blood pressure monitoring for adults with hypertension. Participants will be recruited within a pragmatic network of hospital and community providers; the planned sample is 420 and glycaemic control is the principal endpoint. The protocol prespecifies safety, adherence, and quality-of-life measures and describes procedures for missing observations. The study was not powered to detect uncommon adverse events. Service capacity and local referral practices influenced the observed pattern of care.', '2025-01-28 09:00:00', '2026-05-15 00:00:00', '1', '1', 'Pragmatic randomized controlled trial', '10.5555/medidex.synthetic.0247', 'SYNTH-ISRCTN-0000100', 'Design And Implementation Protocol for home blood pressure monitoring in hypertension', 'English', 'Medidex Synthetic Press') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

